          },
          "text": "🇺🇸🇻🇪Respect for international law and the principles of the UN Charter is essential for global and regional security and must be upheld by all states. Not bombs, but the democratic will of the people of #Venezuela is the way to resolve the country's unfolding crisis. \nThe PES is monitoring the situation after the U.S. attacks near Caracas last night. \nWhile the July 28, 2024, election results announced by authorities aligned with Nicolás Maduro have failed to command broad international confidence, reflecting deeper concerns about democratic legitimacy and respect for fundamental rights, this does not justify military or coercive measures. \nOur solidarity remains with the Venezuelan people, and democracy is the only viable path toward a durable resolution. In the meantime, the safety of EU citizens in the country must be guaranteed."
        },
